IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra-definitions`

-- wra3-sch12.l4: the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, Schedule 12 (supersession of decisions of former
-- appellate bodies). Part wra3, layer 1. Written from inputs/ukpga-2012-5.txt, a plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk
-- (version 2026-07-01), not the official text.
--
-- Host Acts (not among the sources): CSA = Child Support Act 1991; SSA1998 = Social Security Act 1998; CSPSSA = Child
-- Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000. The paragraph numbers of Schedule 12 are not printed in the text. They are
-- counted by cross-heading and by the "is amended as follows" lines (CSA 1991 paras 1 to 3; SSA1998 para 4; CSPSSA para 5):
-- DERIVED and uncorroborated; section 103(1) of this Act (raw line 1661, another part's range) says what the Schedule is for.
-- The definitions the Schedule inserts are encoded over a small type of the bodies they name. The amendments that add "an
-- appeal tribunal or" / "a Commissioner" to a host list of decisions open to supersession are encoded as list limbs: the
-- host lead-ins are not printed, so each answers JUST TRUE for a decision of the named bodies and NOTHING otherwise.

§ `sch 12 the bodies the definitions name`

-- src:3501 | (6) In this section—
-- src:3502 | “appeal tribunal” means an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998 (the functions of which have been transferred to the First-tier Tribunal);
-- src:3503 | “Child Support Commissioner” means a person appointed as such under section 22 (the functions of whom have been transferred to the Upper Tribunal).
@ref sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) (src:3501-3503)
DECLARE `sch 12 body` IS ONE OF
    `sch 12 an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998`
    `sch 12 a person appointed as a Child Support Commissioner under section 22 of the Child Support Act 1991`
    `sch 12 a person appointed as a Social Security Commissioner under Schedule 4 to the Social Security Act 1998`
    `sch 12 a tribunal of persons appointed as Social Security Commissioners`
    `sch 12 any other body`

-- "appeal tribunal" means an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998 (CSA 17(6),
-- CSA Sch 4C para 2(3), SSA1998 10(7), CSPSSA Sch 7 para 4(7): the same words in each).
@ref sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) (src:3502)
GIVEN `the body` IS A `sch 12 body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) the body is an appeal tribunal` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `sch 12 an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“appeal tribunal” means an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998" (a closed definition)
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- "Child Support Commissioner" means a person appointed as such under section 22 (CSA 17(6)).
@ref sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) (src:3503)
GIVEN `the body` IS A `sch 12 body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) the body is a Child Support Commissioner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `sch 12 a person appointed as a Child Support Commissioner under section 22 of the Child Support Act 1991` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Child Support Commissioner” means a person appointed as such under section 22" (a closed definition)
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- "Commissioner" means a person appointed as a Social Security Commissioner under Schedule 4, and includes a tribunal of such
-- persons (SSA1998 10(7), CSPSSA Sch 7 para 4(7)).
-- src:3514 | (7) In this section—
-- src:3515 | “appeal tribunal” means an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of this Part (the functions of which have been transferred to the First-tier Tribunal);
-- src:3516 | “Commissioner” means a person appointed as a Social Security Commissioner under Schedule 4 (the functions of whom have been transferred to the Upper Tribunal), and includes a tribunal of such persons.
@ref sch 12 para 4(3) SSA1998 10(7) (src:3514-3516)
GIVEN `the body` IS A `sch 12 body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 4(3) SSA1998 10(7) the body is a Commissioner` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `sch 12 a person appointed as a Social Security Commissioner under Schedule 4 to the Social Security Act 1998` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 12 a tribunal of persons appointed as Social Security Commissioners` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "means a person appointed ... and includes a tribunal of such persons" leaves open whether anything else is one
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The functions of an appeal tribunal "have been transferred to the First-tier Tribunal", and those of a Commissioner "to the
-- Upper Tribunal" (the parentheses of the definitions).
-- src:3502 | “appeal tribunal” means an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998 (the functions of which have been transferred to the First-tier Tribunal);
-- src:3503 | “Child Support Commissioner” means a person appointed as such under section 22 (the functions of whom have been transferred to the Upper Tribunal).
@ref sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) the functions have been transferred (src:3502-3503)
GIVEN `the body` IS A `sch 12 body`
GIVETH A MAYBE Authority
`sch 12 para 2(3) CSA 17(6) the body whose functions have been transferred is now` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `sch 12 an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998` THEN JUST `the First-tier Tribunal`
    WHEN `sch 12 a person appointed as a Child Support Commissioner under section 22 of the Child Support Act 1991` THEN JUST `the Upper Tribunal`
    WHEN `sch 12 a person appointed as a Social Security Commissioner under Schedule 4 to the Social Security Act 1998` THEN JUST `the Upper Tribunal`
    WHEN `sch 12 a tribunal of persons appointed as Social Security Commissioners` THEN JUST `the Upper Tribunal`
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the parentheses say where the functions of these bodies went, and nothing about any other body
    WHEN `sch 12 any other body` THEN NOTHING

§ `sch 12 decisions that may be superseded`

-- The amendments add the decisions of an appeal tribunal or a Commissioner (CSA 17(1)(b), (d), (e); CSA Sch 4C para 2(1)(c), (2);
-- SSA1998 10(1)(aa); CSPSSA Sch 7 para 4(1)(aa), (2)) to the decisions a host provision lists as open to supersession.
-- Section 103(1) of this Act says the Schedule contains "amendments reinstating powers to make decisions superseding decisions
-- made by appellate bodies before their functions were transferred" (raw line 1661; a lawyer's reading, F-sch12-1).
-- src:3511 | (2) In subsection (1), the “and” at the end of paragraph (a) is repealed and after that paragraph there is inserted—
-- src:3512 | (aa) any decision under this Chapter of an appeal tribunal or a Commissioner; and
@ref sch 12 para 4(2) SSA1998 10(1)(aa) (src:3511-3512)
GIVEN `the body that made the decision` IS A `sch 12 body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 4(2) SSA1998 10(1)(aa) the decision is within the decisions listed as open to supersession` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body that made the decision`
    WHEN `sch 12 an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 12 a person appointed as a Social Security Commissioner under Schedule 4 to the Social Security Act 1998` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 12 a tribunal of persons appointed as Social Security Commissioners` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the amendment adds one limb to a list whose other limbs are in the host Act, which is not among the sources
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:3497 | (2) In subsection (1)—
-- src:3498 | (a) in paragraphs (b) and (d) after “any decision of” there is inserted “ an appeal tribunal or ”;
-- src:3499 | (b) in paragraph (e) after “any decision of“ there is inserted “a Child Support Commissioner or”.
@ref sch 12 para 2(2) CSA 17(1) (src:3497-3499)
GIVEN `the body that made the decision` IS A `sch 12 body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 2(2) CSA 17(1) the decision is within the decisions listed as open to supersession` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body that made the decision`
    WHEN `sch 12 an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 12 a person appointed as a Child Support Commissioner under section 22 of the Child Support Act 1991` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the amendment adds to paragraphs (b), (d) and (e) of a list whose other limbs are in the host Act, which is not among the sources
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:3504 | (1) In Schedule 4C (departure directions), paragraph 2 is amended as follows.
-- src:3505 | (2) In sub-paragraph (1)(c), after “any decision of” there is inserted “ an appeal tribunal or ”.
-- src:3506 | (3) In sub-paragraph (2), after “any decision of“ (in each place) there is inserted “an appeal tribunal or”.
-- src:3507 | (4) After sub-paragraph (2) there is inserted—
-- src:3508 | (3) In this paragraph “appeal tribunal“ means an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998 (the functions of which have been transferred to the First-tier Tribunal).
@ref sch 12 para 3 CSA Sch 4C para 2 (src:3504-3508)
GIVEN `the body that made the decision` IS A `sch 12 body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 3 CSA Sch 4C para 2 the decision is within the decisions listed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body that made the decision`
    WHEN `sch 12 an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the amendment adds "an appeal tribunal or" to a list whose other limbs are in the host Act, which is not among the sources
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:3518 | (1) In Schedule 7 to the Child Support, Pensions and Social Security Act 2000 (housing benefit and council tax benefit), paragraph 4 (decisions superseding earlier decisions) is amended as follows.
-- src:3519 | (2) In sub-paragraph (1), the “and” at the end of paragraph (a) is repealed and after that paragraph there is inserted—
-- src:3520 | (aa) any decision under this Schedule of an appeal tribunal or a Commissioner, and
-- src:3521 | (3) In sub-paragraph (2)—
-- src:3522 | (a) after “the decision appealed against to“ there is inserted “the tribunal or”;
-- src:3523 | (b) after “the decision being appealed against to” there is inserted “ the Commissioner or ”.
-- src:3524 | (4) After sub-paragraph (6) there is inserted—
-- src:3525 | (7) In this paragraph—
-- src:3526 | “appeal tribunal” means an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998 (the functions of which have been transferred to the First-tier Tribunal);
-- src:3527 | “Commissioner” means a person appointed as a Social Security Commissioner under Schedule 4 to that Act (the functions of whom have been transferred to the Upper Tribunal), and includes a tribunal of such persons.
@ref sch 12 para 5 CSPSSA Sch 7 para 4 (src:3518-3527)
GIVEN `the body that made the decision` IS A `sch 12 body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 5 CSPSSA Sch 7 para 4(1)(aa) the decision is within the decisions listed as open to supersession` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body that made the decision`
    WHEN `sch 12 an appeal tribunal constituted under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Social Security Act 1998` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 12 a person appointed as a Social Security Commissioner under Schedule 4 to the Social Security Act 1998` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 12 a tribunal of persons appointed as Social Security Commissioners` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the amendment adds one limb to a list whose other limbs are in the host Act, which is not among the sources
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
